  "body": "## Cause\n`crates/ui/src/build_info.rs` pinned the toolbar's build time (`TOOLBAR_BUILD_UTC`) and source sha (`short_source()`) under `#[cfg(test)]`, but `toolbar_lines` and the narrow version-only label in `panes.rs` rendered the real `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`. The release script commits the version bump after its gate runs, so every cut changed one glyph in three shell snapshots and turned main red (23 px each after 0.15.0).\n\n## Fix\n- New toolbar-only `TOOLBAR_VERSION`: `\"0.0.0\"` under `#[cfg(test)]` (never a released version), the real `VERSION` otherwise.\n- `toolbar_version()` returns `v{TOOLBAR_VERSION}`. `toolbar_lines` uses it, and so does the narrow label in `panes.rs`, which now goes through `build_info` instead of reading `VERSION` directly.\n- The debug-info dialog still shows the real `VERSION`, `BUILT_UTC` and `SOURCE_SHA`, and its tests still assert `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`.\n- The snapshot tests are unit tests in the `camcraft-ui` lib (`egui_app::tests`), so the `cfg(test)` pin applies to the build that renders them.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/449-pin-toolbar-version.md`.\n\n## Tests\n- New: `build_info::tests::toolbar_label_pins_the_test_version_not_the_package_version` checks that the full and compact top lines read `v0.0.0 · test` and that `toolbar_version()` returns `v0.0.0`, whatever `CARGO_PKG_VERSION` is.\n- Snapshots regenerated once (`UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1`, CWD `crates/ui`): `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png`. Pixel diff against main: 177 px each, all inside the top-right badge (x 1224-1253, y 25-33). The badge now reads `v0.0.0` and nothing else in the images changed.\n- Gate (CWD `crates/ui`): `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` gave 316 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored, including the three snapshot tests and the debug_info tests. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- Not exercised: the `crates/ui/tests/` integration binaries. They are untouched, and the only non-test change is the narrow-label string source.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #449\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
